From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brody Franks <brody@franks.id.au>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:02:25 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wgengine: clean up when NewUserspaceEngine fails

NewUserspaceEngine deferred cleanup while the resource list was still
empty. A failed start could leave the TUN, UDP sockets and Linux policy
rules behind.

Read the final list on rollback. Close the router before the device and
release the owned network monitor, DNS manager and BIRD client. Start
the WireGuard shutdown watcher only once the engine is complete. Return
the startup error first, followed by any errors from cleanup in order.

On Linux, record the rule families claimed at startup. Repair only
claimed families that are still usable. Drain router event handlers
before taking the router lock and serialize rule repair with teardown.
The first Close attempts every teardown step, even if the interface
cannot be brought down. Release the claim after that attempt so later
closes leave a replacement interface and its rules alone.

On Windows, clear the firewall only if this router requested firewall
work. On FreeBSD, build the NAT rules before installing references to
the shared anchor. Track cleanup from the first attempted anchor load.
A partial load or failed removal gets one final attempt at close.

Change-Id: I913286a95a245286eeab14ddaaa8d77e361a5e11
Signed-off-by: Brody Franks <brody@franks.id.au>
